<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  athena.entitlements — Hardened Runtime entitlements for the Athena daemon
  (ADR 024 Tier 1 / process lockdown).

  Threat model: a co-resident malicious process that scrapes the daemon's
  address space (task_for_pid() → mach_vm_read()) to read the resident model
  weights, KV cache, or decrypted secrets. The single biggest defense is to
  ship WITHOUT `get-task-allow`, under the Hardened Runtime, so AMFI denies the
  task port to any caller that is not Apple-entitled against a target that
  permits attach. See docs/decisions/024-*.md.

  Notes on what is deliberately ABSENT:
    * com.apple.security.get-task-allow = false (below) — the lever. A dev/adhoc
      build effectively carries get-task-allow=true; this overrides that.
    * NO com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation — the binary is
      statically linked (only weak platform dylibs from /usr/lib/swift), so
      library validation is a non-issue. Granting it would needlessly widen the
      attack surface.
    * NO com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory —
      MLX's Metal kernels load from a precompiled `default.metallib` resource;
      no CPU-side JIT is performed. Spike B (Phase 0) confirmed metallib loads
      under the Hardened Runtime with none of these granted.

  This file is consumed by deploy/build.sh's signing step and asserted by
  deploy/verify-hardening.sh.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.get-task-allow</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
